From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:00:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] moe-cache-x1: GLM-5.3 NVMe expert streaming, x12..x21
 measured source

Lane source as built for build-x21 (sha256 E25B87BE...6A30) and measured in
cells-x12..x21: glm5-next arch with ssm read bank=true (correctness fix, x7),
cooperative matvec (x12), NVMe sibling pre-read default ON (x15/x16), two-drive
identical-copy split, per-node submission v2 (opt-in), READBACK_CACHED host
readback default ON (x20/x21), moe-disk-probe and moe-trace tools.
All measured arms EXACT against the no-draft baseline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit f63e3dd4e8944e26e970dbce84f53be7b634bafc)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (moe-cache-x1); no upstream origin exists.
